        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Strength and Power: Neuromuscular Adaptations",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nMUSCLE ARCHITECTURE:\n  PARALLEL FIBER:\n    Fibers run parallel to force production axis.\n    +---------+\n    |   | | | |\n    |   | | | |\n    |   | | | |\n    +---------+\n    Force    = N_fibers × force_per_fiber\n    Velocity = Vmax of individual fiber (fast)\n    Examples: biceps brachii, sartorius\n    Best for: velocity and range of motion."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-STRENGTH-POWER.md#028",
      "path": [
        "03-STRENGTH-POWER.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:sports-science:03-strength-power, git-history:sports-science:03-strength-power]",
        "canonical_path": "sports-science/03-STRENGTH-POWER.md",
        "concepts": "[strength, power]",
        "current_path": "sports-science/03-STRENGTH-POWER.md",
        "id": "maxim:sports-science:strength-power",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "sports-science",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[strength, power]",
        "section": "sports-science",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Strength and Power: Neuromuscular Adaptations",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PENNATE FIBER (single, bi-, or multi-pennate):\n    Fibers at an angle to the force production axis.\n      +----------+\n      |  /  /  / |\n      | /  /  /  |\n      |/  /  /   |\n      +----------+\n      Force    = N_fibers × force_per_fiber × cos(θ)\n      Velocity = reduced (angle effect)\n    Pennation angle θ: typically 5–25° at rest; increases with load.\n    Examples: vastus lateralis, gastrocnemius, tibialis anterior\n    Best for: high force production.\n    More fibers packed into same volume → more total force."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-STRENGTH-POWER.md#029",
      "path": [
        "03-STRENGTH-POWER.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:sports-science:03-strength-power, git-history:sports-science:03-strength-power]",
