        "current_path": "sports-science/03-STRENGTH-POWER.md",
        "id": "maxim:sports-science:strength-power",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "sports-science",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[strength, power]",
        "section": "sports-science",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Strength and Power: Neuromuscular Adaptations",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PHYSIOLOGICAL CROSS-SECTIONAL AREA (PCSA):\n    PCSA = (mass × cos θ) / (density × fiber length)\n    True measure of force-producing capacity.\n    Different from anatomical CSA (which does not account for pennation).\n    Why it matters: two muscles with same anatomical CSA can produce\n    very different forces if pennation angles differ.\n```"
    },
