      "text": "TRAINING IMPLICATION:\n  To train Type IIx (fast, high-force) fibers, effort must be maximal\n  OR fatigue must be reached so that Type I fibers are exhausted and\n  Type II fibers are forced into action (high reps to failure also\n  recruits large motor units by this mechanism).\n  Both heavy loading and high-rep-to-failure recruit Type II fibers —\n  different physiological routes to the same neuromuscular target."
